@@ -0,0 +1,65 @@
+# Omega-Zero RetroAchievements development build
+
+Base: oauramos/omega-zero PR #33, commit 2192ba96575452bf3403e9f566ec7af30760fbbb.
+Achievement service and memory bridge adapted from pvaibhav/slot commit
+b3473670b03a3fd29eefb5fdcded53669122c748, GPL-3.0-or-later.
+The vendored rcheevos evaluator retains its MIT licence in
+crates/omega-achievements/vendor/rcheevos/LICENSE and licenses/rcheevos-MIT.txt.
+
+## Scope
+
+- Softcore GB, GBC and GBA, using the existing mGBA/gpSP cores.
+- Background account login, ROM identification, cached evaluation, atomic unlock
+  persistence and online submission, including deferred offline submission.
+- Queued text unlock panels using Omega's existing visual style.
+- Existing LCD/grid/dot shaders, overlays and cartridge artwork retained.
+- Missing configuration leaves achievements disabled.
+- No browser, hardcore, leaderboards, badge/chime presentation or SNES tracking yet.
+- SNES/PS1 bypass the wrapper and background ROM preparation. Future SNES support
+  needs a verified RA memory map, header-aware ROM hashing and real-core tests.
+
+## Validation before device testing
+
+Local Rust check and clippy target Omega's device feature. Achievement-service
+unit tests use fake servers, not real credentials or live achievement submissions.
+The memory integration test executes original tiny GB/GBC/GBA programs through
+real mGBA/gpSP cores and checks their RA-addressed memory. The ARM workflow repeats
+this using the exact cores built from Omega's pinned source and patches.
+None of these checks establish live account acceptance or handheld performance.
+
+## First installation, only after the cloud job passes
+
+1. Copy the ENTIRE existing Omega card to your Mac. Verify the backup can be read.
+2. Keep the known-working shader executable outside the card.
+3. Copy only the new omega-zero executable to the card's existing System directory.
+   Do not overwrite your Config, Games, Saves, Labels or Overlays folders.
+4. First boot with no Config/retroachievements.toml file. Confirm normal gameplay,
+   shaders, save/load and return to the shelf still work.
+5. With the device off, copy retroachievements.toml.example into Config, rename it
+   retroachievements.toml, and enter your credentials locally. Never upload this
+   filled file to GitHub or paste it into chat. An emulator login token can be
+   used instead of a password; a Web API key is not the correct token.
+6. Ensure the handheld's clock is correct and connect Wi-Fi on the shelf.
+7. Use one RA-supported ROM and a disposable save for the first live test.
+   Verify an easy unlock on the RetroAchievements website. A popup alone does not
+   prove the server accepted the award.
+8. Exercise suspend/resume, rewind, save/load, reconnect and an ordinary shutdown.
+
+The service writes Config only when YOU create its configuration. It stores
+credentials, caches and pending unlocks under Saves/RetroAchievements. Normal game
+save locations and formats are unchanged by this port. Keep that achievement
+folder when backing up: it can contain unsynced unlocks and a private login token.
+
+## Rollback
+
+Power off and restore System/omega-zero from the shader backup. That restores the
+program, not earlier versions of saves/settings. Remove or rename the RA config
+if you want achievements disabled on a later test boot. Do not delete the RA
+cache until pending awards are synced or backed up.
+
+## Reproduce
+
+Apply retroachievements.patch to the base commit above with git apply. Use the
+supplied retroachievements.yml workflow in your own fork to run tests and compile
+on a GitHub ARM runner. This changes neither the upstream repository nor the
+existing LCD Grid Build workflow.
